<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/insights/">← Back to insights</a><div class="section-label">Strategy · Featured</div><h1>Why 73% of MSMEs Stall at ₹50 Crore — and How to Break Through</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body"><p>Most Indian businesses hit an invisible ceiling somewhere between ₹20Cr and ₹50Cr revenue. Founders often attribute this to market saturation, lack of capital, or increased competition. In most cases, they are wrong.</p><h4>The Real Reason: Organisational Debt</h4><p>When a business grows from ₹5Cr to ₹50Cr, it does so largely on the strength of its founder and a handful of key people. Processes are improvised. Decisions are centralised. Systems are informal. This works — until it doesn't.</p><p>At some threshold, usually around ₹30–50Cr revenue, the complexity of the business exceeds the capacity of informal coordination. Orders start falling through cracks. Quality becomes inconsistent. Key hires take too long to become productive. The founder is overwhelmed and the business cannot scale without them.</p><h4>The Diagnostic Framework</h4><p>We use a simple 4-question diagnostic to identify where the ceiling is:<br>1. Can your business run for 2 weeks without you making a major decision?<br>2. Do you have documented SOPs for your top 10 business processes?<br>3. Do you have a KPI dashboard your leadership team reviews weekly?<br>4. Can a new hire become 80% productive within 30 days?</p><p>If the answer to any of these is no, you have identified your ceiling. The good news: all four are solvable — and the order in which you solve them matters enormously.</p><h4>The Breakthrough Sequence</h4><p>Based on our engagements, the right sequence is: (1) Document critical processes first. (2) Build the performance measurement system. (3) Delegate decisions with clear accountability. (4) Then and only then, scale headcount or geography.</p><p>Most founders attempt this in the wrong order — they hire first, then wonder why the problems multiply.</p></div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
